er of the spring vegetable was someone in the house, but I couldn't figure out who. It can't be said that everyone in the house is on good terms, but although there may be some small desires, I can't imagine that someone would make threatening and killing the next Tetsujou-sama... such a thing.\" [644] Daijing's fellow guest, Jumo, also nodded with a disappointed expression. He was also a member of the Kuzunoha family, and had thought about it many times like Daijing. [645] Suspecting a family member is painful. But killing among family members is not an abnormal thing. Of course, just two months ago, Shima didn't think so either. His father even killed his mother because he found her annoying. He could easily kill someone for a mistress and insurance money. Shima never thought of such a thing for even a second. And he never thought he would kill his father. [646] But now it's different. Shima has experienced firsthand that family members will also kill each other. Perhaps that's why he found himself calmly observing them as soon as he entered the room. [647] Oyim probably realized that asking further questions wouldn't lead to progress, so he sighed lightly:\n[648] \"I would like to ask a somewhat impolite question, but is the next successor, the Kakuzaki house, really so important? Major, so important that the killer is willing to kill the Spring Vegetable girl to prevent her from succeeding?\" [649] \"It's not so much important as it is terrifying. People outside the village will never understand, but for this village, the Kakuzaki house is indeed equivalent to a god. This mansion, this mountain, this village, all exist for the Kakuzaki house, and that's not an exaggeration.\" [650] \"You mean there shouldn't be anyone trying to harm them because it's terrifying?\" [651] Daimy\u014d nodded. Indeed, when considering the villagers' doubts and sighs in the Dragon's Pond, as well as the hostile glances when Shin'ichi was suspected, and the villagers' participation in