cted it from the beginning.\" [3568] \"Suzume-san probably doesn't know that Satsuki-san's phone was stolen. The police have deliberately kept it under wraps. I think the killer probably convinced her that her own phone was broken and borrowed Satsuki's phone instead.\" [3569] \"That's too despicable!\" [3570]\n[3571] Sutsumi spat angrily. His face was flushed with anger, and he seemed truly angry. As a seasoned detective, Sutsumi was a person who showed his emotions openly, unlike the former Aso and others. [3572] \"However, this clearly proves that the killer contacted Lady Moon beforehand. It seems that the killer had been waiting for an opportunity since three days ago and spoke to Lady Moon yesterday when it was raining.\" [3573] \"Damn it! We planned to observe the situation, so we didn't stop Snowy's phone, but it turned out to be counterproductive! However, now that we can calculate the call time, we can pinpoint the killer.\" [3574] \"Honestly, I don't think we should expect too much. The killer knows this too, so the phone call was probably made around the time of Snowy's funeral. Especially, Lady Moon might have changed the name in the resume from 'Snowy' to the killer's name, so I think the killer checked the phone after the murder. However, the killer left the resume unchanged, indicating that they didn't care about this line of inquiry and believed it wouldn't lead to them.\" [3575] \"This guy is getting smarter. Of course, it's not appropriate to say this to a killer who has killed six people in succession.\" [3576] \"Maybe it's even worse than 'smart'.\" [3577] \"What's wrong?\" asked Jirou. [3578] \"The books in the bookshelf are knocked over.\" [3579] Jirou looked and saw that four books in the topmost row of the bookshelf that reached the ceiling were upside down. [3580] \"That's strange. I saw them arranged neatly a few days ago.\" [3581] Ogami approached the bookshelf and reached up to take down one of the inverted books. It was likely a volume of the Kotoharu school's teachings. Since it was written in ancient Chinese characters and the handwriting was messy, Shibumi couldn't even read the title. [3582] \"It seems to be a diary of the Kotoharu school during the Edo period. There are records of various ceremonies everywhere, but these four books seem to be from different eras and don't seem to have any connection.\" [3583] Ogami suddenly stopped flipping through the books. [3584] \"Mr. Suzu, for safety's sake, please check all the books here.\" [3585] \"Did you find something?\" [3586] Yuri remains silent and silently hands the open book to Sakata. [3587] \"Oh!\" Sakata exclaims.\n <Assistant> I have read the book and I will answer the question you ask."